# Handoff before code

The handoff comes from `plugin-ui-ux-design`. The words come from `plugin-ux-writing`. The accessibility requirements come from `plugin-accessibility`. If one of the three is missing, write nothing and name it.

Read `references/angular.md` only when the project already has `angular.json` or `@angular/core`. That file does not choose Angular. Taiga UI is used only when the project already depends on it.

Core Web Vitals, field data, 75th percentile, mobile and desktop reported apart: LCP at or under 2.5 s, INP at or under 200 ms, CLS at or under 0.1 (web.dev, current set).
